.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-admin-operators - Who holds the operator role; grant it, revoke it (lists when run bare)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 admin operators [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List the operator grants, newest first: the account that holds each, who granted it
(empty for a grant made out of band, by the seeds or the gateway's own maintenance task),
the note it was given with, and when it expires.

.PP
Expired grants are listed too, as history. A grant opens the operator surface while its
expiry is empty or still ahead and its account is active.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for operators


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 admin operators
  rail0 admin operators --pretty
  rail0 admin operators grant 019e748b-… --note "on call this week" --expires 7d
  rail0 admin operators revoke 019e748b-…
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-admin(1)\fP, \fBrail0-admin-operators-grant(1)\fP, \fBrail0-admin-operators-revoke(1)\fP
